     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "The function never returns a 0 for any value of n."
    },
    {
     "id": 1329856,
     "content_html": "no result / infinite computation",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "There are 2 base cases in the function, one for n &lt; 0 and one for n == 0. Since n started as a positive number, n will never be less than 0. Therefore, the n == 0 base case is reached and the function completes successfully."
